{
  "id": "binomial-theorem-oq-02-oq-01-oq-01",
  "name": "Multinomial PMF and MGF formalization",
  "status": "completed",
  "knowledge": {
    "insights": [
      "PMF integration requires lifting the multinomial theorem from ℝ to ℝ≥0∞ (ENNReal); done via Fintype.sum_equiv onto a piAntidiag sum + Finset.sum_pow_eq_sum_piAntidiag",
      "Composition type (k : α → ℕ with Σk = n) is the natural support; its Fintype instance is transport along an Equiv with ↥(s.piAntidiag n)",
      "The absorption identity kᵢ·multinomial(s,k)=n·multinomial(s, kᵢ−1) is a single combinatorial engine: a no-division ℕ proof cancelling (kᵢ−1)!·∏_{j≠i}kⱼ! after Nat.multinomial_spec",
      "Mean and cross moment both reduce, via ONE Finset.sum_nbij' bijection lowering kᵢ, to the multinomial theorem on n−1 trials; the kⱼ factor in the cross moment rides along unchanged (j≠i), so E[XᵢXⱼ]=n·pᵢ·(mean of Xⱼ at n−1)=n(n−1)pᵢpⱼ",
      "Marginal of Xᵢ is Binomial(n,pᵢ): reindex compositions with kᵢ=m onto compositions of n−m on s∖{i} (zero the i-th coord), Nat.multinomial_insert splits off C(n,m), and ∑_{j≠i}pⱼ=1−pᵢ",
      "Covariance Cov(Xᵢ,Xⱼ)=−n·pᵢ·pⱼ reflects the simplex constraint ΣXᵢ=n (negative correlation)",
      "Variance Var(Xᵢ)=n·pᵢ(1-pᵢ) and the full covariance matrix Cov(Xᵢ,Xⱼ)=n·pᵢ(δᵢⱼ-pⱼ) (= n·(diag(p)-p·pᵀ)) completed in child binomial-theorem-oq-02-oq-01-oq-01-oq-04 (verified, 0-axiom), via a diagonal second factorial moment by absorption + routing the off-diagonal through the existing covariance theorem."
    ],
    "builtItems": [
      "BinomialTheoremOQ02OQ01OQ01.lean: 707-line fully verified formalization (0 sorries, 0 axioms; #print axioms lists only propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound)",
      "Composition type + Fintype instance; multinomialPMFVal and multinomialPMF (PMF.mk) in ENNReal",
      "multinomialPMF_sum_eq_one (normalization), multinomialPMF_apply, multinomialPMF_support — all proved",
      "multinomial_absorb (absorption identity) + multinomial_absorb_weighted (real-weighted form)",
      "multinomial_marginal_binomial, multinomial_mean (E[Xᵢ]=n·pᵢ), multinomial_cross_moment, multinomial_covariance — all proved",
      "Replaced native_decide with decide in the dice example to keep the file axiom-free; deleted the now-redundant Aristotle companion"
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [
      "Mathlib has no multinomial *distribution* in its PMF library (this file supplies one)",
      "No ENNReal-level multinomial theorem wrapper (worked around via Nat.cast onto Finset.sum_pow_eq_sum_piAntidiag)",
      "No multinomial absorption identity kᵢ·multinomial=n·multinomial(kᵢ−1) (built here from Nat.multinomial_spec)"
    ],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Optional follow-up: package the absorption identity and the marginal/mean/covariance lemmas for a Mathlib contribution",
      "Optional follow-up: variance Var(Xᵢ)=n·pᵢ·(1−pᵢ) and the full covariance matrix; MGF/PGF of the multinomial"
    ],
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE (verified): the multinomial distribution is a genuine Mathlib PMF, with marginal=Binomial(n,pᵢ), mean=n·pᵢ, and covariance=−n·pᵢ·pⱼ all proved from a single absorption-identity engine. 707 lines, 0 sorries, 0 axioms."
  },
